date-released: "2026-08-15"

abstract: >
  LQL-Equiv-web computes biologically equivalent doses in external-beam
  radiotherapy under the linear-quadratic-linear model: biologically effective
  dose, equivalent dose in a reference fractionation, normal-tissue
  complication probability, tumour control probability and radiation-induced
  cancer risk, with corrections for incomplete inter-fraction repair,
  proliferation and treatment protraction. It is a Python and browser-based
  successor to the 2014 MATLAB application, compared case by case against it.
  For research and education only; not a medical device.

keywords:
  - radiotherapy
  - biologically effective dose
  - linear-quadratic-linear model
  - equivalent dose
  - NTCP
  - TCP
  - medical physics
  - Python
  - Streamlit

